1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,840
If you've started skipping walks or avoiding stairs because you're worried about falling, that worry itself might be raising your risk more than your legs are.

2
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:19,360
Geriatric researchers call this the fear-of-falling cycle — cutting back on activity to feel safer lets your muscles and balance reflexes weaken from disuse, which then makes an actual fall more likely.

3
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:29,760
The CDC reports that about 1 in 4 adults over 65 falls every year, and doctors now screen for this fear-avoidance pattern specifically, not just raw leg strength.

4
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:34,720
First, the fix isn't avoiding activity — it's structured balance and strength training.

5
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:45,600
A review in the British Journal of Sports Medicine found programs combining both cut fall rates by up to 34%, while walking-only routines showed almost no benefit for falls specifically.

6
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:53,200
Single-leg stands and sit-to-stand repeats, done two to three times a week, rebuild both the confidence and the reflexes at once.

7
00:00:53,520 --> 00:01:00,800
Second, most falls happen at home, not outside, so a safer space does more for your confidence than caution alone.

8
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:12,800
Loose rugs, dim lighting, and walking around in socks or backless slippers are common triggers — securing rugs, adding grab bars near the tub, and switching to shoes with real tread indoors make a real difference.

9
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:16,000
Third, medications matter more than people think.

10
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:25,360
The CDC's STEADI program specifically flags sedatives and several blood pressure drugs, and the risk climbs sharply once you're taking four or more at the same time.

11
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:31,120
An annual review with a doctor or pharmacist catches risky combinations before they cause a fall.

12
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:38,400
Fall risk isn't just about your legs — fear-driven inactivity, home hazards, and medications all feed into each other.

13
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:42,800
Handle them one at a time, and both the risk and the fear drop together.
